        "id": 0,
        "original_id": "876efd37-88a1-5204-b640-6210783d775d",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- People: Alfred L. Werker, Jon Jost, Del Andrews, Erich von Stroheim, Boots Mallory, ZaSu Pitts\n- Companies: Fox Film Corporation\n- Films: Ridin' the Wind, Hello, Sister!, Stolen Harmony, All the Vermeers in New York\n- Roles: film director, independent filmmaker\n\nFacts:\n- Alfred L. Werker was born on December 2, 1896, and he was a film director whose work in movies spanned from 1917 through 1957.\n- Alfred L. Werker worked in film production jobs and assistant directing before co-directing his first film, Ridin' the Wind, with Del Andrews in 1925.\n- Fox Film Corporation executives brought Alfred L. Werker in to re-shoot and re-edit Erich von Stroheim's 1933 film Hello, Sister!, which co-starred Boots Mallory and ZaSu Pitts.\n- Stolen Harmony was directed by Alfred L. Werker, and the movie climaxes with an exciting car chase.\n- Jon Jost was born on 16 May 1943 in Chicago, and he is an American independent filmmaker.\n- Jon Jost wrote, directed, and produced the 1990 American film All the Vermeers in New York.\n- Alfred L. Werker died on July 28, 1975.",
        "type": "TextSummary"
      },
      {
        "id": 1,
        "original_id": "344164d5-c60a-5359-9c68-3519c0ff1e25",
        "text": "Page: Alfred L. Werker. Sentence: Alfred L. Werker (December 2, 1896 – July 28, 1975) was a film director whose work in movies spanned from 1917 through 1957.\nPage: Alfred L. Werker. Sentence: After a number of film production jobs and assistant directing, Werker co-directed his first film, \"Ridin' the Wind\" in 1925 alongside director Del Andrews.\nPage: Alfred L. Werker. Sentence: He was brought in by Fox Film Corporation executives to re-shoot and re-edit Erich von Stroheim's film \"Hello, Sister!\nPage: Alfred L. Werker. Sentence: \" (1933), co-starring Boots Mallory and ZaSu Pitts.\nPage: Jon Jost. Sentence: Jon Jost (born 16 May 1943 in Chicago) is an American independent filmmaker.\nPage: Stolen Harmony. Sentence: The movie climaxes with an exciting car chase and was directed by Alfred L. Werker.\nPage: All the Vermeers in New York. Sentence: All the Vermeers in New York is a 1990 American film written, directed and produced by Jon Jost.",
